<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="CH8x3403-en-63b7a58d" type="transl"><teiHeader><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Remnants of Ch'in Law</title><editor role="translator">Hulsewé</editor></titleStmt><publicationStmt><ab>published electronically as part of the TLS project at https://hxwd.org</ab><availability status="2"><ab>This work has been licensed for use in the TLS</ab></availability></publicationStmt><sourceDesc><bibl><title>Remnants of Ch'in Law</title>1985</bibl><ab>Translation of <bibl corresp="#CH8x3403"><title xml:lang="och"/></bibl> into <lang xml:lang="en">English</lang>.</ab></sourceDesc></fileDesc><profileDesc><creation resp="#schwermann">Initially created: <date>2025-11-11T22:50:42.866+09:00</date> by schwermann</creation></profileDesc></teiHeader><text><body><div><head>Translated parts</head><p xml:id="CH8x3403-start"><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:38:49.202+09:00">a report in writing is to be made concerning the favoured crop</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:39:45.113+09:00">Whenever it rains when the crop is already fully grown,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:41:23.714+09:00">and the number of ch'ing which were affected are to be reported in writing.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:41:53.782+09:00">floods,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:42:37.234+09:00">or other creatures which damage the crops,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:52:10.736+09:00">Nearby prefectures have lightfooted runners deliver the letter,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:40:33.598+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.19" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-11T23:01:04.73+09:00">the number of ch'ing concerned is always to be reported in writing.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.21" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-11T23:01:36.301+09:00">Nearby prefectures have lightfooted runners deliver the letter,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.23" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-11T23:02:25.699+09:00">distant prefectures have the courier service deliver it.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.27" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-11T23:03:13.025+09:00">By the end of the eighth month ... it.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.29" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-11T23:03:34.319+09:00">Statutes on Agriculture.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.1" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:37:20.538+09:00">Whenever the rain is beneficial</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:37:42.275+09:00">and affects the grain in ear</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:54:30.481+09:00">and the grain in ear, as well as the number of ch'ing [4.6 hectare] of cultivated fields and areas without crops.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:41:21.22+09:00">also the quantity of rain </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:42:22.595+09:00">Likewise, in cases of drought and violent wind or rain, </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:51:30.228+09:00">the number of ch'ing concerned is always to be reported in writing.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:52:45.672+09:00">distant prefectures have the courier service deliver it.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Maren.Ziegler-Bellenberg" modified="2025-11-25T22:20:48.228+09:00">By the end of the eighth month .... it.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-16T19:53:39.448+09:00">Statutes on Agriculture.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-1a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#schwermann" modified="2025-11-18T23:07:09.148+09:00">hordes of grasshoppers</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Maren.Ziegler-Bellenberg" modified="2025-11-25T22:15:30.89+09:00">one should not venture to cut timber in the forests or block water courses. </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T19:50:07.142+09:00">Except in the months of summer</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T19:50:38.628+09:00">one should not venture to burn weeds to make ashes,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T19:51:28.989+09:00">to collect [indigo],</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T19:51:40.922+09:00">young animals, eggs or fledglings. </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T19:51:59.526+09:00">One should not ...... poison fish or tortoises </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T19:52:10.778+09:00">or arrange pitfalls and nets. </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T19:52:26.439+09:00">By the seventh month (these prohibitions) are lifted.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T19:53:25.495+09:00">Only when someone has unfortunately died and one fells (wood for) the inner and outer coffins,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T19:54:27.166+09:00">this is not done according to the seasons.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T19:53:55.731+09:00">In settlements close to corrals and other forbidden parks,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.1" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T21:25:37.799+09:00">In the second month of spring</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T21:28:35.231+09:00">in the season of young animals one should not venture to take dogs to go hunting.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Maren.Ziegler-Bellenberg" modified="2025-11-25T22:18:59.992+09:00">When dogs of the common people enter forbidden parks without pursuing and catching animals,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T21:30:55.14+09:00">one should not venture to kill them;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T21:31:15.263+09:00">those which pursue as well as catch animals </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T21:31:26.339+09:00">are to be killed. </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T21:31:49.853+09:00">Dogs killed by the wardens</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T21:32:08.019+09:00">are to be completely handed over to the authorities;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T21:33:56.547+09:00">of those that are killed in other forbidden parks </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T21:34:33.67+09:00">the flesh may be eaten, but the skin is to be handed over.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-2a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-11-25T21:34:43.392+09:00">Statutes on Agriculture.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-3a.1" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-12-08T20:59:17.165+09:00">The delivery of hay and straw per ch'ing </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-3a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-12-08T20:59:43.274+09:00">is to be done according to the number of fields bestowed.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-3a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-12-08T21:00:07.045+09:00">Irrespective of whether the fields are cultivated or uncultivated</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-3a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-12-08T21:00:36.415+09:00">the delivery per ch'ing is three bushels of hay</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-3a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-12-08T21:01:10.406+09:00">(or) two bushels of straw.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-3a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-12-08T21:02:32.581+09:00">From a raking of hay or a bundle of whitlow grass upward, everything will be received.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-3a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-12-08T21:03:44.932+09:00">When delivering hay and straw,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-3a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-12-08T21:05:18.929+09:00">is allowed.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-3a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-12-08T21:05:25.112+09:00">substitution of the one for the other </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-3a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2025-12-08T21:05:55.903+09:00">Statutes on Agriculture.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-4a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:09:07.82+09:00">Whenever (from a storehouse for) grain, hay or straw the wood and the (bottom) matting have been removed, the number of bushels is to be reported to the Prefect's court.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-4a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:09:57.879+09:00">Do not use it; </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-4a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:10:05.128+09:00">cover it again with the matting.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-4a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:10:35.81+09:00">Statutes on Agriculture.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-5a.1" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:11:59.934+09:00">As regards rations for (official) carriage horses and draft oxen,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-5a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-27T21:27:19.442+09:00"> if for more than two months rations have not been issued </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-5a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:13:16.125+09:00">they are all to be stopped;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-5a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-27T21:27:49.548+09:00">or forwarded.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-5a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:14:01.189+09:00">Those who are given rations by the Main (Office of) Agriculture without having a permanent record</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-5a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:15:53.814+09:00">one must not exceed (the stipulations of) the certificate.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-5a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:16:30.258+09:00">are to be given rations as from the day of the arrival of the certificate;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-5a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:17:21.662+09:00">Statutes on Agriculture.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-6a.1" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:18:44.203+09:00">Commoners living in farms should not venture to sell wine.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-6a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:18:54.745+09:00">The Agricultural Overseer</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-6a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:19:10.306+09:00">and the Division Assistants carefully restrain and stop them.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-6a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:19:25.887+09:00">Persons who do not obey the Ordinances will have committed a crime.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-6a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-13T09:19:37.261+09:00">Statutes on Agriculture.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-5a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-27T21:27:21.925+09:00">or forwarded,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_001-5a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-01-27T21:27:40.231+09:00">they must not be issued</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.1-h" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-05-04T23:04:43.594+09:00"/><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-05-04T22:52:50.786+09:00">7th,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-05-04T22:53:07.889+09:00">10th</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-05-04T22:55:48.119+09:00">and 1st month the oxen used in agriculture are measured;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.1" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-05-04T23:04:38.869+09:00">In the 4th,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-05-04T23:26:27.278+09:00">when the year is ended,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-05-04T23:26:56.926+09:00">in the last month they are subject to a great evaluation,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-05-04T23:27:53.948+09:00">the corral keepers are relieved of one turn of duty</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-05-04T23:28:10.191+09:00">and the chief of the cattle men is granted in days three decades.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-05-19T16:19:38.913+09:00">the Overseer of Agriculture is granted a bottle of wine and a bundle of dried meat;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-05-19T16:19:48.938+09:00">For good results</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_010-4a.1" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-06-06T16:31:01.576+09:00">Let the prefectural and the general offices select willows as well as other wood that is soft and can be used for writing,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_010-4a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-06-06T16:30:59.202+09:00">and make it square in order to write on it;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_010-4a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-06-06T16:31:23.299+09:00">when there are no square (pieces), use "boards".</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_010-4a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-06-06T16:31:34.278+09:00">In prefectures where there are many sedges in the hills,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_010-4a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-06-06T16:31:41.73+09:00">write on sedge tied together;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_010-4a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-06-06T16:31:55.107+09:00">where there is no sedge, use rushes,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_010-4a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-06-06T16:32:01.314+09:00">stitchted together with hemp.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_010-4a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-06-06T16:32:15.972+09:00">All these should be piled up when there are many to be harvested.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_010-4a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-06-06T16:32:28.229+09:00">(Statutes concerning) the Controller of Works</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:23:17.58+09:00">For bad results</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:23:55.992+09:00">the Overseer of Agriculture is berated,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:24:46.577+09:00">the corral menials are fined two months.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:25:43.93+09:00">In case the oxen have been used in agricultural work</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:26:08.091+09:00">and they have decreased in girth,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:26:55.765+09:00">the person in charge is bastinadoed with ten strokes for each inch.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:27:49.48+09:00">They (viz. the oxen) are also evaluated per village.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:28:03.956+09:00">For good results</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:28:45.475+09:00">the Village Chief is granted in days one decade;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-06-13T20:47:20.601+09:00">for bad results he is bastinadoed with thirty strokes.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-1a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:30:07.981+09:00">Statutes on Stables and Parks</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-2a.1" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:31:12.122+09:00">When loaned iron tools</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-2a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:32:04.004+09:00">that have become worn, spoilt and unusable, break,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-2a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:33:12.268+09:00">this has to be noted in writing;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-2a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:33:33.886+09:00">they are to be taken in without charging.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-2a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:33:41.227+09:00">Statutes on Stables and Parks</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.1" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:34:47.672+09:00">When government horses and cattle are taken out to graze,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.2" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:35:08.107+09:00">and horses (or cattle) die,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.3" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-07-13T17:56:33.256+09:00">the prefecture where they have died is to be speedily informed.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.4" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:36:29.972+09:00">The prefecture speedily inspects this and collects it (viz. the dead animal).</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.5" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:37:00.748+09:00">In case this is not done speedily and it becomes spoilt, </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.6" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-06-23T18:50:03.308+09:00">the Prefect refunds it with the value it had before it was spoilt. </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:37:37.217+09:00">If small bond-servants die of sickness, </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:38:09.008+09:00">this is to be reported to ... concerned.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:38:20.781+09:00">For those who die without having been ill, </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.10" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:38:42.347+09:00">this is to be reported to the office by means of an investigation report to judge it.  </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.11" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:39:02.424+09:00">When horses or oxen of the Great Stables, </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.12" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:39:13.197+09:00">the Palace Stables</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.13" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-07-13T22:48:50.255+09:00">or palace stables are concerned,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.14" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:39:51.543+09:00">their sinews,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.15" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:39:57.284+09:00">hides</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-07-13T22:49:42.58+09:00">and horns as well as their value in cash are to be handed over;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-07-13T22:49:45.233+09:00">the persons concerned take these to the office concerned.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-07-13T22:49:52.392+09:00">When those who use government horses and oxen lose horses (or oxen) ... the prefecture where they have died;</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#matejkas" modified="2026-07-14T18:20:51.44+09:00">the prefecture investigates and .... sells the meat.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:41:31.006+09:00">It immediately collects the sinews, </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.21" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:41:39.186+09:00">hides</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.22" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:41:46.614+09:00">and horns,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.23" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:42:03.205+09:00">as well as fully collecting its value in cash. </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.24" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-07-14T00:31:29.644+09:00">In case the money (collected) is less than (the sum stipulated by) the Statute, </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.25" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:43:00.576+09:00">orders are given to the person(s) concerned to make good the deficiency, meanwhile informing the office.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.26" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-07-14T00:31:32.429+09:00">The office informs the prefecture (responsible for) the horses or oxen to remove (the animals from the register).</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.27" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:46:30.648+09:00">Now, as regards the evaluation</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.28" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-07-14T00:42:30.199+09:00">of oxen officially used by the prefectures and by the general offices, these will be evaluated once each.</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.29" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-07-14T00:42:25.601+09:00">If after a full year</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.30" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:47:19.95+09:00">one third has died of (a number of) ten or more, </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.31" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:47:46.132+09:00">or, if not fully ten oxen,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.35" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:49:00.42+09:00">and the Assistant Prefect are all guilty.  </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.36" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:49:21.353+09:00">The Ministry of Finance evaluates the prefectures,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.37" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-07-14T00:44:24.829+09:00">(whereas) the Great Granary evaluates the general offices as well as those who had received oxen for use. </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.32" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:50:54.957+09:00">as well as for those who have received oxen for use, three ormore have died after a full year, </seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.33" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#Runtian" modified="2026-06-06T20:51:10.954+09:00">the officials in charge,</seg><seg corresp="#CH8x3403_CHANT_002-3a.34" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#AMeiner" modified="2026-07-14T00:42:40.014+09:00">the men who fed the oxen, as well as the Prefect</seg></p></div></body></text></TEI>